# Apache .htaccess — Shikkha24
#
# Replaces the former Cloudflare Pages _headers file (removed 2026-09-14).
# Source: docs/security.md §5 (security headers + CSP).
#
# TWO CSP PROFILES (docs/security.md §5): a strict one for static / editorial
# pages, and a relaxed one for ad-bearing and interactive pages, because AdSense
# needs inline scripts and dynamic script injection.
#
# ⚠️ Apache does NOT have the Cloudflare comma-join problem. Apache's `Header
# set` replaces the value cleanly — no `!`-detach trick is needed. The former
# Cloudflare `_headers` `! Content-Security-Policy` syntax is gone.
#
# ⚠️ **Path matching in .htaccess is done with `SetEnvIf Request_URI`, never with
# `<LocationMatch>`.** Apache permits <Location>/<LocationMatch> in server and
# virtual-host context only; using them in .htaccess is a core parser error that
# returns **HTTP 500 on every request**. The previous revision used them, and the
# JS harness of the day reimplemented the regex matching instead of exercising
# Apache, so it passed while the file was unrunnable. Verified against a real
# Apache 2.4 by `pnpm verify:apache` — do not change the mechanism without
# re-running it.
#
# ⚠️ **Production check:** confirm an ad-bearing page returns exactly ONE
# Content-Security-Policy header with the relaxed policy. A pattern that fails to
# match fails **silently** — the page still returns 200, just under the strict
# policy, and AdSense is blocked with no error anywhere.
#
# ⚠️ **`cms.shikkha24.com` is a PLACEHOLDER hostname.** It is the CMS origin AND
# the media origin (media on DianaHost disk since 2026-09-12). A CSP cannot be
# templated, so this literal host MUST match the production `PUBLIC_CMS_ORIGIN`
# and `PUBLIC_MEDIA_BASE_URL` exactly. It is currently a placeholder because the
# CMS hostname is still pending DNS.
#
# S9 changes, recorded so the diff is not a mystery later:
#   • `img-src` / `media-src` now name the CMS host, not the retired R2 host —
#     every article image would otherwise be blocked in production
#   • `connect-src` now names the CMS host in the STRICT profile too, because the
#     newsletter signup sits in the footer of every page and the comment,
#     citizen and bookmark surfaces post to the CMS from editorial pages
#   • `/article/*` gains `frame-src` for the click-to-load video embeds
#   • `/gallery` and `/gallery/*` were REMOVED from the relaxed list: the gallery
#     carries no ad slot (none of the eight approved `AD_POSITIONS` is a gallery
#     slot) and no inline script, so the strict profile is sufficient and
#     tighter. If a gallery ad slot is ever approved, add both rules back.
#
# S11 change (2026-09-13), recorded for the same reason:
#   • The article rule moved from `/article/*` to `/:category/:id/:slug`, following
#     the URL architecture change (`docs/seo-plan.md` §2). This is NOT cosmetic —
#     `/article/*` would have stopped matching every article page, silently
#     dropping them to the strict profile and blocking AdSense site-wide.
#   • `/article/:slug` is now a redirect stub and deliberately keeps the strict
#     profile (no script, no ad slot).
#
# S12 change (2026-09-15): the route dispatch was rewritten from `<LocationMatch>`
# to `SetEnvIf Request_URI` + `Header ... env=`, and the two dead `<FilesMatch>`
# cache rules were replaced with the same mechanism. See `docs/security.md` §5.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Route → CSP profile. Tag the ad-bearing routes; the headers below consume the
# tags. `SetEnvIf` and `Header` are both FileInfo-level overrides, which is what
# a cPanel host grants.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<IfModule mod_setenvif.c>
  # Homepage — 4 ad slots + poll + newsletter
  SetEnvIf Request_URI "^/(\?.*)?$" SHIKKHA24_CSP_RELAXED=1

  # Category listing — 1 ad slot. Also /category/:slug/page/:n (4 segments).
  SetEnvIf Request_URI "^/category/[^/?#]+(/page/[0-9]+)?/?(\?.*)?$" SHIKKHA24_CSP_RELAXED=1

  # Live blog — 1 ad slot + the refresh island
  SetEnvIf Request_URI "^/live/[^/?#]+/?(\?.*)?$" SHIKKHA24_CSP_RELAXED=1

  # Quiz — 2 ad slots
  SetEnvIf Request_URI "^/quiz(/[^/?#]+)?/?(\?.*)?$" SHIKKHA24_CSP_RELAXED=1

  # Article — 3 ad slots + comments + bookmarks + video embeds.
  #
  # Exactly three path segments. This is the article route and *only* the article
  # route: `/:category/:id/:slug`. Every other route in the tree is 1, 2 or 4
  # segments (`/category/:slug/page/:n` is 4). Do NOT add an exclusion list of
  # reserved roots here — an earlier revision excluded `study-abroad`, which is
  # both a 2-segment listing and the first segment of real article URLs, so every
  # study-abroad article silently fell to the strict profile.
  #
  # If a future route introduces a non-article 3-segment path, `pnpm verify:apache`
  # turns red: it reads each page's own JSON-LD to decide the expected profile, so
  # it does not share this rule's blind spots.
  SetEnvIf Request_URI "^/[^/?#]+/[^/?#]+/[^/?#]+/?(\?.*)?$" SHIKKHA24_CSP_ARTICLE=1
</IfModule>

<IfModule mod_headers.c>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Strict profile — the default for every route
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# `style-src 'unsafe-inline'` is required by Astro's inline stylesheets
# (`build.inlineStylesheets: 'auto'` in astro.config.mjs). It is the only
# relaxation in this profile — scripts stay strict.
#
# `connect-src` names the CMS because the newsletter signup form is in the
# footer of every page and posts to it. The form is not rendered at all unless
# `PUBLIC_CMS_ORIGIN` is set, so an unconfigured deploy makes no such request —
# but the policy has to allow it for the configured one.

  Header always set Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload"
  Header always set X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
  Header always set Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
  Header always set Permissions-Policy "geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()"
  Header always set X-Frame-Options "DENY"
  Header always set Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://cms.shikkha24.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cms.shikkha24.com; media-src 'self' https://cms.shikkha24.com; frame-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Relaxed profile — the routes tagged above.
#
#   /                     homepage — 4 ad slots + the poll + newsletter
#   /:category/:id/:slug  article  — 3 ad slots + comments + bookmarks + video embeds
#   /category/*           category — 1 ad slot (and /category/*/page/*)
#   /live/*               live blog — 1 ad slot + the refresh island
#   /quiz, /quiz/*        quiz     — 2 ad slots
#
# Every other route keeps the strict policy, which is the point of two profiles.
# That includes `/article/:slug` (since S11 a 200-OK redirect stub with no script
# and no ad slot), `/gallery` (no ad slot, no inline script), `/bookmarks` (no
# CMS call at all — the list is browser-local) and `/citizen` (posts to the CMS,
# which the strict `connect-src` already allows).
#
# ⚠️ The two tags are mutually exclusive by construction, so a response carries
# exactly one of these two headers. `set` replaces, and the article rule is last
# so it wins if a route ever matched both.
#
# The AdSense loader only injects the library when a real AdSense unit exists, and
# the islands only call the CMS when the reader taps something — so today these
# routes still make zero third-party requests. The relaxation costs nothing until
# the features are actually used.
#
# `frame-src` on the article rule is for the video embed, which is click-to-load:
# the iframe is created only after the reader taps play, so no third-party request
# is made on page load. `youtube-nocookie.com` is used deliberately — it sets no
# tracking cookie until playback.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Header always set Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://cms.shikkha24.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.gstatic.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://cms.shikkha24.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; media-src 'self' https://cms.shikkha24.com; frame-src https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.google.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests" env=SHIKKHA24_CSP_RELAXED
  Header always set Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://cms.shikkha24.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.gstatic.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://cms.shikkha24.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; media-src 'self' https://cms.shikkha24.com; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://www.youtube.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.google.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests" env=SHIKKHA24_CSP_ARTICLE

</IfModule>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cache rules
#
# ⚠️ `<FilesMatch>` matches the **basename**, not the path, so it cannot express
# "/_astro/*" — `<FilesMatch "\._astro/">` and `<FilesMatch "^/fonts/">` never
# matched a single file and both rules were dead. They are `SetEnvIf Request_URI`
# now. `<FilesMatch "\.html$">` genuinely is a basename rule and stays.
#
# These use `Header set` (not `always`) so a 404 is not cached for a year.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<IfModule mod_setenvif.c>
  # Hashed build assets are content-addressed — cache them forever.
  SetEnvIf Request_URI "^/_astro/" SHIKKHA24_IMMUTABLE=1
  # Self-hosted fonts are content-stable; re-fetching them is pure waste.
  SetEnvIf Request_URI "^/fonts/" SHIKKHA24_IMMUTABLE=1
</IfModule>

<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable" env=SHIKKHA24_IMMUTABLE

  # HTML must revalidate so a publish is visible as soon as the batch window closes.
  <FilesMatch "\.html$">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
